==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|hvar}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hwar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kʰvaːr/|lang=is}}
* {{IPA|/xʷaːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aːr|lang=is}}

===Adverb===
{{is-adv|-}}

# [[where]] (of location)
#: '''''Hvar''' áttu heima?''
#:: '''Where''' do you live?
#: '''''Hvar''' [[vera niðurkominn|er hann niðurkominn]]?''
#:: What’s become of him?
#: '''''Hvar''' í ósköpunum varstu, Óskar?''
#:: '''Where''' in heaven’s name were you, Óskar?

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* [[finna hvar skórinn kreppir]] (to [[feel where the shoe pinches]])
* [[hér og hvar]] ([[here and there]])
{{der-mid}}
* [[sýna hvar Davíð keypti ölið]]
* [[víðast hvar]] (almost [[everywhere]])
{{der-bottom}}

